.TH KARVI-DAEMON 1 "" "karvi"
.\" Paths and options are not hyphenated, and lines are not stretched.
.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
karvi\-daemon \- manage the private per\-user daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED SYNOPSIS: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon start\fR [\-\-foreground]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon stop\fR [\-\-grace | \-\-after=DURATION | \-\-force]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon restart\fR [\-\-grace | \-\-after=DURATION | \-\-force]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon status\fR [\-\-format text|json]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon serve\fR
.\" END GENERATED SYNOPSIS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" BEGIN GENERATED DESCRIPTION: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
.PP
Without an option, stop and restart refuse while the daemon reports active
jobs. \-\-grace drains the daemon, so it rejects new jobs, and waits for active
jobs to finish. \-\-after=DURATION drains and waits until jobs finish or DURATION
elapses, whichever comes first, then forces the stop. \-\-force stops at once;
unfinished work still receives terminal records. Interrupting a wait leaves the
daemon draining. \-\-help shows this text. Specified, not yet available:
daemon start \-\-start\-timeout DURATION.
.PP
A daemon is compatible when its version and its IPC schema both equal the
client's; either difference is incompatible. An upgraded client never submits
a job to, kills, or silently replaces an incompatible running daemon. Status
and explicit stop/restart use the stable same\-UID lifecycle envelope for
released IPC schemas, allowing an operator to recover after an upgrade without
reinstalling the older karvi executable.
.\" END GENERATED DESCRIPTION
.SH FILES
.TP
.I BASEDIR/socket/daemon.sock
The daemon's socket, the operator's alone
.RB ( daemon.socket ).
.TP
.IR BASEDIR/state/daemon.json ", " BASEDIR/logs/daemon.log
Its state and its log.
.PP
A job runs under the configuration of the client that submitted it, sent in
its plan; the daemon's own configuration, its launching invocation's, serves
the process alone: the
.B daemon.*\&
keys, the
.B basedir
of its socket, state, and log, and the sweeps at its start.
A key whose reload class is
.B daemon\-start
reaches a running daemon at its next start.
.PP
A daemon a client launched passes on a filtered environment:
.BR HOME ,
.BR USER ,
.BR LOGNAME ,
.BR PATH ,
the names in
.BR security.child\-environment\-allowlist ,
every
.B KARVI__
variable,
.BR KARVI_ASKPASS_PATH ,
.BR TZ ,
and
.BR TMPDIR ,
so
.B NETPASS
never reaches it; the client resolves credentials and hands them over per
job.
After
.B daemon.shutdown\-idle\-timer
(1h) with no job and no request but a status, the daemon stops itself,
exit 0, with a
.B stopping: idle
line in its log, and the next run launches another; 0 never stops.
A service unit runs it with the timer at 0, since
.B Restart=on\-failure
does not restart a clean exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR karvi (1),
.BR karvi\-job (1),
.BR karvi\-watch (1),
